                "username": "garybeihl"
            },
            "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\nAbandoning \u2014 Patrick is right, this was an environment artifact on my end, not a real break in spdm.\n\nRoot cause: my local checkout had a stale vendored subprojects/sdbusplus pinned at ff73d3d (2026-04-09). The wrap is revision=HEAD, but meson reuses an existing subproject directory rather than re-fetching it, so my build compiled against Apr-9 sdbusplus \u2014 which predates sdbusplus::match_rules (promoted to the top-level namespace in 89560) and the shorter Mapper::get_sub_tree_t alias. That produced the errors this change \"fixed\". A clean checkout, as CI uses, fetches current sdbusplus (HEAD has both symbols) and spdm main builds fine \u2014 I confirmed match_rules is absent at ff73d3d and present at current HEAD, and that updating the subproject resolves it.\n\nWorse, this change reverts the shorter-aliases migration (eae7d72), which is the opposite of the intent. Abandoning. Apologies for the noise, and thanks for catching it."
        },
        {
